#!/usr/bin/env zsh
source "$HOME/.zshrc" >/dev/null 2>&1
unalias cc 2>/dev/null || true
cc() { claude --dangerously-skip-permissions "$@"; }
cc -p --model claude-opus-5 --effort max --permission-mode bypassPermissions --output-format stream-json --verbose --session-id b8a5ec03-3e03-49e2-8955-0a426f20cfbf $'<challenge>\nCreate an unforgettable landing page for a fictional premium brand called **Elysian**.\n\nUse these four images to shape the visual world of the experience:\n\n- https://code.melvynx.dev/elysian-classical-surreal-still-life.png\n- https://codelynx.mlvcdn.com/uploads/2026-07-13/2026-07-13-greco-roman-scholarly-landscape.png\n- https://codelynx.mlvcdn.com/uploads/2026-07-13/2026-07-13-vibrant-mountain-river-valley.png\n- https://codelynx.mlvcdn.com/uploads/2026-07-13/2026-07-13-golden-temple-starry-night.png\n\nThe experience should feel imaginative, editorial, luxurious, and slightly surreal. It should make a strong impression immediately and reveal more personality through interaction and movement.\n</challenge>\n\n<creative-freedom>\nAlways prioritize creativity. Make bold, unexpected decisions and develop an original concept rather than following familiar landing-page conventions.\n\nYou have complete creative freedom over the story, copy, layout, typography, colors, transitions, and interactions. Use the images in whatever way creates the strongest experience: crop them, layer them, sequence them, transform them, or make them part of the interaction.\n\nDo not place the images into ordinary rectangular sections and call the page finished. Treat them as raw material for a coherent visual world. Avoid generic startup layouts and generic component-library aesthetics.\n</creative-freedom>\n\n<delivery>\nBuild the complete experience in the current repository. It must work beautifully on desktop and mobile.\n\nDo not explain the design before building it. Make the creative decisions yourself and deliver the most original, polished result you can.\n</delivery>\n\nWork only inside the current working directory. Do not edit files outside the current working directory.\n\nUse pnpm exclusively if dependency installation or package scripts are needed. Do not use npm.\nSet the browser title and the primary visible title to your model name, using only identity information already available to you. Add nothing else to either title.\nRun the relevant checks yourself. Do not edit files outside the current working directory.' 
